Final Interview Answer

"In my project, developers push code to GitHub, which triggers a Jenkins pipeline. Jenkins builds the application using Maven, creates a Docker image, scans it with Trivy, tags it with the build number, and pushes it to Amazon ECR. Kubernetes running on AWS EKS then pulls the image and deploys it using rolling updates. 
We monitor the running containers with Prometheus, Grafana, and CloudWatch, and if an issue occurs, we roll back to a previous stable image."
